# Source: https://github.com/Bioconductor/GenomicFeatures/issues/73
# Symptom: TSS-to-promoter extension on chrM (16569 bp) produces negative
#   chromStart values and chromEnd values exceeding chromosome length.
#   Generated by R GenomicFeatures when no chromosome size clamping is applied.
#   chrM is a common trouble spot because the mitochondrial genome is circular
#   and short; genes near the origin produce promoter windows that wrap past 0.
#   Distinct from negative_start_coordinate.bed (that uses a non-mitochondrial
#   example); this variant specifically documents the chrM/circular genome edge case.
chrM	-924	1076	MT-TF_promoter	0	+
chrM	-853	1147	MT-RNR1_promoter	0	+
chrM	15523	17523	MT-ND6_promoter	0	-
